        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "@hosaka,\n\n> Is there a setting that controls the autocomplete border? At least winborder and pumborder seem to have no effect.\n\nYes, setting something like `vim.o.pumborder = 'single'` works. Needs Neovim>=0.12 (current Nigthly).\n\n> How does one disable the autocomplete for shell `:!` commands?\n\nBy setting appropriate `config.autocomplete.predicate`, as [mentioned here](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-cmdline.html#minicmdline.config-autocomplete). I believe the `:!` case is already covered in its example. To see more available completion types, see `:h :command-complete`.\n\n---\n\n> I feel like showing the peek window for search-and-replace (e.g. `:%s`) is pretty useless/annoying. Especially with `inccommand=split`.\n\n@lithammer, I did have a thought on not showing peek window if the range is the whole buffer. But decided not to do that for consistency reasons.\n\nBut I see how this can conflict with `inccommand=split`. At the very least, adding something like `config.autopeek.predicate` might be useful here. The default can then not peek if `inccommand=split` is set and the command uses it.\n\nI'll think about it.\n\n",
