            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> What I noticed is that I cannot delete the selected entry. For example, in the recording below, I am unable to delete the word \"picker.\"\n\nWhat is the output of `:=vim.o.wildmode`? It is probably something like `longest:full` or contains \"longest\" in some form. This is not a [suggested option value](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-cmdline.html#module-suggestedoptionvalues).\n\nFor this to happen, there needs to be an explicit setting of 'wildmode' option either before or after `require('mini.cmdline').setup()`. Removing that should fix the issue.\n\n---\n\nThere is no stronger wording on this option value, since `longest:full` also technically works. And you can remove the whole word with `<C-w>`, by the way.",
