            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> autocorrect seems not comptiable with cabbrev, defined a cabbrev by `vim.keymap.set(\"ca\", \"F\", \"Flogsplit\", {})`, without`mini.cmdline`, run `:F` will run `:Flogsplit`, with `mini.cmdline`, run `:F` will run `:f`.\n\nYes, it doesn't seem to work consistently at least. In my regular config this abbreviation works (probably because I have other user command that starts with `F`), but on a clean config it works as you describe.\n\nTechnically, this can be worked around by tweaking [`config.autocorrect.func`](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-cmdline.html#minicmdline.config-autocorrect): make it return input word directly if it is one of the \"special\" ones. But I guess taking a more careful approach here and not autocorrect at all if the word is a Command-line mode abbreviation makes sense. I'll take a look.",
